152 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 61 0 R/T(The Analysis :  Sales data is in the order_items table, while category names are in the products table. I joined them on product_id and grouped the results by category. For each category I summed sale_price, counted item rows and averaged retail_price, then sorted by sales and kept the top five.)/E(The Analysis :  Sales data is in the order_items table, while category names are in the products table. I joined them on product_id and grouped the results by category. For each category I summed sale_price, counted item rows and averaged retail_price, then sorted by sales and kept the top five.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[30]>>
endobj

153 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 61 0 R/T(Insight  Outerwear & Coats \($200K\) and Jeans \($193K\) led 2024 and made up about 54% of the top five\220s sales. Jeans almost caught Outerwear at a 33% lower price because it sold 44% more items. Swim sold a lot of items \(1,755\) but at the lowest price sell \($56\), while Suits sold the fewest \(816\) sell at $129. Suggestion :  For Q4,We could push the top two, bundle Swim to raise basket size, and find out why Suits sells so little.)/E(Insight  Outerwear & Coats \($200K\) and Jeans \($193K\) led 2024 and made up about 54% of the top five\220s sales. Jeans almost caught Outerwear at a 33% lower price because it sold 44% more items. Swim sold a lot of items \(1,755\) but at the lowest price sell \($56\), while Suits sold the fewest \(816\) sell at $129. Suggestion :  For Q4,We could push the top two, bundle Swim to raise basket size, and find out why Suits sells so little.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[31]>>
endobj

